# Finite catalogue of the faces of the explicit polytope

There are 1069 nonempty entries: 144 singletons, 404 pairs, 390
quadrilaterals, 130 eight-vertex facets, and the complete vertex set.
At this stage these are finite sets of vertex labels.  `FaceRealization`
proves that they are precisely the geometric exposed faces.

`faceFlag` gives a full strictly increasing chain through each entry;
`supportRows` gives at most four original supporting inequalities whose
common equality labels are the entry.  `codeFace` uses base-three digits
0 for a free coordinate, 1 for zero, and 2 for one, with coordinate zero
the least significant digit.

This file is generated by `scripts/generate_face_data.py` from the exact
coordinate certificate. Its data are audited by Lean in `FaceDataChecks`.
Balanced index dispatch keeps lookup efficient during kernel reduction;
every leaf is an explicit finite set or vector.
-/

